AB  - Domain shift presents a significant challenge in machine learning (ML) applications. Ensuring high prediction quality in real-world scenarios requires robust handling of out-of-distribution (OOD) data. To address this, we propose a novel ensemble learning framework tailored for multi-sensor systems, adaptable to a wide range of dataset variations. The framework integrates hyperparameter tuning and model selection directly into the training process, enabling efficient training of deep ensembles. Leveraging the power of deep ensembles, the framework not only enhances in-distribution accuracy but also effectively detects OOD data and domain shifts. We evaluated the framework using five publicly available datasets, achieving an average in-distribution accuracy of 98%, with OOD accuracy dropping to 57%. Additionally, the framework’s OOD detection capability achieved an average area under the receiver operating characteristic curve (AUROC) of 91%.
