AB  - Aiming at the problem of"shortcut learning” and cross-domain generalization failure in unmanned aerial vehicle (UAV) type recognition in non-cooperative environment, this paper proposes a new RF feature modeling framework based on hardware decoupling and feature invariance optimization (Surgery $+\mathbf{M I} \times \mathbf{F I}^{\mathbf{3}}$). The framework extracts high signal-to-noise ratio baseband data from the original intercepted signal through statistical threshold blind signal separation and adaptive down-conversion technology. Based on the construction of a 62-dimensional panoramic feature space covering time, frequency and nonlinear domains, this paper proposes a hardware decoupling mechanism to ensure that the individual sensitive features that lead to overfitting of the model are removed from the physical level. Subsequently, by introducing a nonlinear penalty strategy that combines mutual information and feature stability, a common fingerprint of the model with cross-domain robustness is purified, and a robust UAV model recognition method is designed based on this. The experimental results show that the recognition accuracy of this method can be improved by more than 40% compared with the original feature recognition method in cross-individual scenarios. At the same time, the recognition rate of various mainstream classifiers is stable at more than 86% under the condition of only $\mathbf{3 0}$-dimensional feature input, which has generalization performance and engineering practical value in complex multipath environment.
